- table Chunk: no longer in the closure — the closest declaration, Manifest, carries 1 of its 6 identities, below the half needed to call it a rename, so this baseline no longer covers it [warn]
- table OpLogLine: no longer in the closure — no declaration carries any of its identities, so this baseline no longer covers it [warn]
- table OpNote: no longer in the closure — no declaration carries any of its identities, so this baseline no longer covers it [warn]
- table OpQueued: no longer in the closure — no declaration carries any of its identities, so this baseline no longer covers it [warn]
- table TextRef: no longer in the closure under that name; CardText carries 1 of its 2 identities, so it is judged as the rename it looks like [warn]
- table OpRecord: has_result, has_timers removed and result, timers added in one edit — if that is a rename the wire id moved with the name and every stored value orphans: declare it `result ... | was = "has_result"`, and pair `json = "has_result"` if the text key must survive (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §5, §16.4) [warn]
- table QueuedChange: entry_bytes removed and entry added in one edit — if that is a rename the wire id moved with the name and every stored value orphans: declare it `entry ... | was = "entry_bytes"`, and pair `json = "entry_bytes"` if the text key must survive (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §5, §16.4) [warn]
- table CardText: size removed and text added in one edit — if that is a rename the wire id moved with the name and every stored value orphans: declare it `text ... | was = "size"`, and pair `json = "size"` if the text key must survive (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §5, §16.4) [warn]
